Tests, made deterministic (bugfix round 0.7). xrfg_layer_two_layers_deep_hold_arming_single (review finding 3 on 0080)
failed on fast PCs every time: the fake runtime slept 250 ms per private swapchain, four per layer, so arming ended
about 1080 ms into a run whose last frame is at about 870 ms on such a PC, and no synthetic frame could come. The
creation now lasts until the frame that names one layer alone was submitted (past the first frame's 400 ms wait,
bounded at 5 s) and the rest come at once, so the remaining frames always see the swapchains armed.
xrfg_layer_presenter_stall expects exactly one presenter stall (result 950); in the first phase, two at a time beside
other builds, a second real stall was seen (a=1, then a=4 11 s later), alone it passes: it is labelled pacing (0091).

